import{_ as a,o as i,c as r,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.BZO4qERu.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Changelog","description":"","frontmatter":{"outline":2},"headers":[],"relativePath":"changelog.md","filePath":"changelog.md","lastUpdated":1791997268000}'),n={name:"changelog.md"};function o(s,e,l,d,c,h){return i(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="changelog" tabindex="-1">Changelog <a class="header-anchor" href="#changelog" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Changelog&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Features, improvements, and upgrade notes, from the first demo to PaperSeek 1.0.0-beta2.</p><h2 id="v1-0-0-beta2" tabindex="-1">1.0.0-beta2 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v1-0-0-beta2" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.0.0-beta2 {#v1-0-0-beta2}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A maintenance release. Reviews and search rankings now carry on when a model gets part of its answer wrong, running searches stay in your history, and Docker Compose is private to your machine by default. It upgrades 1.0.0-beta1 in place, without a migration.</p><h3 id="reviews" tabindex="-1">Reviews <a class="header-anchor" href="#reviews" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reviews&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>A review no longer fails because a few papers come back without usable evidence. Those papers are left out of the outline and marked in the paper list; the rest of the review goes ahead, and preparing the outline again retries only them.</li><li>A paper keeps every quote that matches its abstract, even when the model gets another quote wrong. Quotes stitched together with an ellipsis (…) are checked as separate passages instead of being rejected.</li><li>The outline no longer stops on a paper without checked evidence. That paper is dropped from the plan, and a paragraph left without sources is given new ones from the checked evidence.</li></ul><h3 id="search-ranking" tabindex="-1">Search ranking <a class="header-anchor" href="#search-ranking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Search ranking&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>When the model scores only some of the candidates, the scores it gave are kept and only the missing papers are asked for again. Papers that still have no score are listed after the scored ones in their original order, and the search reports a warning.</li><li>&quot;Why it ranks&quot; explanations are requested in smaller groups, so long explanations, Chinese ones especially, are no longer cut off. Papers a reply skipped are asked for once more.</li></ul><h3 id="history" tabindex="-1">History <a class="header-anchor" href="#history" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;History&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Queued and running searches now appear in the search history, also after you reload the page, and cannot be deleted while they run.</li></ul><h3 id="self-hosting" tabindex="-1">Self-hosting <a class="header-anchor" href="#self-hosting" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Self-hosting&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>The supplied Docker Compose file publishes PaperSeek on this machine only (127.0.0.1:8765). To open it from other devices, set <code>PAPERSEEK_HOST=0.0.0.0</code> in <code>.env</code> and protect access; <code>PAPERSEEK_PORT</code> still changes the port.</li><li>The MCP Docker image builds again from a clean checkout.</li><li>Third-party notice tables display correctly in every distribution.</li></ul><h3 id="documentation-site" tabindex="-1">Documentation site <a class="header-anchor" href="#documentation-site" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Documentation site&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>On the home page, a resting finger or the end of a trackpad swipe no longer jumps to another section.</li></ul><h3 id="upgrade-notes" tabindex="-1">Upgrade notes <a class="header-anchor" href="#upgrade-notes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Upgrade notes&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>From 1.0.0-beta1, install 1.0.0b2 with pip or set <code>PAPERSEEK_VERSION</code> to <code>1.0.0-beta2</code> for Docker; your data needs no migration. See <a href="./self-hosting/upgrade#from-an-earlier-1-0-beta">upgrading from an earlier 1.0 beta</a>.</li><li>If you reach a Docker deployment from another device, take the new <code>compose.yaml</code> and set <code>PAPERSEEK_HOST</code> as described above.</li></ul><h2 id="v1-0-0-beta" tabindex="-1">1.0.0-beta1 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v1-0-0-beta" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1.0.0-beta1 {#v1-0-0-beta}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>PaperSeek 1.0.0-beta1 is a <strong>complete architectural refactor with breaking changes</strong>. It rebuilds the execution model, frontend, storage boundaries, and distribution around a shared research application, with an explicit migration path for existing user data.</p><h3 id="three-modules-and-independent-histories" tabindex="-1">Three modules and independent histories <a class="header-anchor" href="#three-modules-and-independent-histories" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Three modules and independent histories&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>A redesigned workspace: Search, Bibliometrics, and Reviews in a collapsible sidebar with each module&#39;s history, and the account at the bottom.</li><li>Settings pages for model APIs, data sources, general preferences, and the user&#39;s data: clear saved keys or all history, each after typing a confirmation phrase. Running tasks are stopped before history is cleared.</li><li>Preliminary bibliometrics over the actually retrieved deduplicated candidate corpus; native-field coverage, keyword co-occurrence, bounded bibliographic coupling, cached networks, and independent exports. LLM scoring remains a subset.</li><li>Review citation evidence alongside papers, outline, and draft; new reviews preserve available source graph snapshots.</li><li>Rename history records; the original question and settings stay unchanged.</li></ul><p>Install it from pip as <code>1.0.0b1</code>; the Docker image tag is <code>1.0.0-beta1</code>.</p><h3 id="paperseek-online" tabindex="-1">PaperSeek online <a class="header-anchor" href="#paperseek-online" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;PaperSeek online&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Sign in for PaperSeek Service: built-in models, no keys, and free daily credits during the public beta (20 a day). A search or an analysis uses 1 credit and a review 5, deducted when the task starts; a failed or cancelled task returns them.</li><li>Your own key: save model connections and data-source keys to your account in Settings; tasks then use your API and no credits. Every data source that takes a key (OpenAlex, PubMed, Semantic Scholar, Google Scholar, Web of Science) requires one in this mode; arXiv, Crossref, and PaperHub work without.</li><li>Without signing in, run one temporary search with your own key typed into the form. It is held in memory only and never saved.</li></ul><h3 id="architecture-rebuilt-around-clear-responsibilities" tabindex="-1">Architecture rebuilt around clear responsibilities <a class="header-anchor" href="#architecture-rebuilt-around-clear-responsibilities" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Architecture rebuilt around clear responsibilities&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Separate <code>paperseek_core</code> for retrieval, query iteration, citation expansion, ranking, and source/model protocols; <code>paperseek_app</code> for run submission, execution, persistence, and queries; and deployment adapters for Community and the online edition.</li><li>Use one application layer across Web, CLI, HTTP API, and MCP. The search core is independent of FastAPI, authentication, SQLite, and Supabase.</li><li>The online edition and Community share one search implementation and the same research pages.</li><li>Rebuild the frontend with Vue 3, TypeScript, and Vite. Shared research pages use the versioned <code>/api/v1</code> contract; generated API types keep frontend and backend interfaces aligned.</li><li>Use explicit asynchronous workflows and httpx clients, with Pydantic models at the boundaries. Retire obsolete runtime entry points.</li></ul><h3 id="persistent-tasks-cancellation-and-recovery" tabindex="-1">Persistent tasks, cancellation, and recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#persistent-tasks-cancellation-and-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Persistent tasks, cancellation, and recovery&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Make saved searches database-backed runs with worker leases, ordered events, checkpoints, and result artifacts. Community can resume compatible interrupted work from committed checkpoints.</li><li>Restore saved pages from a run snapshot and replayed events, then follow updates through SSE. Reconnecting the browser does not submit a new search.</li><li>Coordinate cancellation and lease ownership so an obsolete worker or a late provider response cannot commit results after cancellation.</li><li>Separate source/model failures from persistence failures: optional retrieval or ranking stages can report warnings and fall back, while a failed result commit cannot be presented as success.</li><li>Introduce versioned SQLite migrations through Alembic and explicit migration commands. Community uses SQLite and local files. A signed-out online search is temporary and is not added to history.</li></ul><p>Community can run the API and an embedded worker as one local service, or run them separately. Reconnecting the browser restores the page; an interrupted task resumes from its checkpoint.</p><h3 id="a-complete-research-workspace" tabindex="-1">A complete research workspace <a class="header-anchor" href="#a-complete-research-workspace" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A complete research workspace&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Vue 3 interface with English and Chinese, consistent navigation, and task-stage progress.</li><li>Question-driven query iteration, bounded retrieval, relevance ranking, and transparent search history.</li><li>Eight scholarly source integrations, with source-specific fields and access settings.</li><li>Local fusion, Embedding + Rerank, and System One preliminary-ranking options.</li><li>Citation expansion and an interactive citation map through OpenAlex.</li><li>Saved runs, filtering, selection, and complete CSV/JSON exports.</li><li><strong>Experimental</strong> abstract-based reviews with editable outlines, section writing, versions, citations, and Markdown/Word/BibTeX exports.</li></ul><h3 id="one-application-several-entry-points" tabindex="-1">One application, several entry points <a class="header-anchor" href="#one-application-several-entry-points" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;One application, several entry points&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The Web UI, six-command CLI, versioned HTTP API, and independent same-version MCP adapter reuse the same application services. Community keeps data in local SQLite and files. The online product adds accounts, service models, queueing, and isolated storage.</p><h3 id="upgrade-notes-1" tabindex="-1">Upgrade notes <a class="header-anchor" href="#upgrade-notes-1" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Upgrade notes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Python <strong>3.12+</strong> is required. Old Python imports, internal APIs, frontend endpoints, and retired CLI/configuration entries are not retained. Supported 0.2 data and environment settings have explicit migration commands; migrated configuration uses the new names without a legacy runtime fallback. See the <a href="./self-hosting/upgrade">migration guide</a> and <a href="./developers/contributing#architecture">architecture notes</a>.</p><p>Search uses abstracts and metadata provided by the source. Standalone cross-source abstract and citation-count enrichment are no longer part of the configuration.</p><h2 id="v0-2-1" tabindex="-1">0.2.1 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v0-2-1" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.2.1 {#v0-2-1}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>July 5, 2026 · Provider routing and hosted service updates</p><h3 id="models-and-retrieval" tabindex="-1">Models and retrieval <a class="header-anchor" href="#models-and-retrieval" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Models and retrieval&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Expanded provider routing with NVIDIA NIM and OpenRouter support.</li><li>Updated PaperHub query handling and candidate-pool narrowing.</li></ul><h3 id="reliability" tabindex="-1">Reliability <a class="header-anchor" href="#reliability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Reliability&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Corrected NVIDIA reranker endpoint handling and improved ranking fallbacks.</li><li>Added retries for transient API failures.</li><li>Unified shared LLM route logging across providers.</li></ul><h3 id="documentation" tabindex="-1">Documentation <a class="header-anchor" href="#documentation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Documentation&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Expanded PaperSeek Service documentation, including hosted data-source credentials and release notes.</li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/paperseek/paperseek/releases/tag/v0.2.1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Original release notes</a></p><h2 id="v0-2-0" tabindex="-1">0.2.0 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v0-2-0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.2.0 {#v0-2-0}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>July 4, 2026 · More sources and multi-lane retrieval</p><h3 id="search-and-ranking" tabindex="-1">Search and ranking <a class="header-anchor" href="#search-and-ranking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Search and ranking&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Expanded the source lineup with arXiv, Semantic Scholar, PubMed, computer-science conferences, and Crossref.</li><li>Introduced source-specific queries, intent recognition, and feedback across query iterations.</li><li>Added preliminary ranking before LLM scoring. Retrieval combines relevance, influence or citations, freshness, and local quality signals, using RRF, BM25/term coverage, and local hashing embeddings.</li><li>Added optional OpenAI-compatible embedding and reranker services.</li></ul><h3 id="online-accounts" tabindex="-1">Online accounts <a class="header-anchor" href="#online-accounts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Online accounts&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Updated email registration and sign-in, with GitHub and ModelScope OAuth.</li><li>Introduced a daily allowance of 20 successful searches for signed-in users at that release.</li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/paperseek/paperseek/releases/tag/v0.2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Original release notes</a></p><h2 id="v0-1-1" tabindex="-1">0.1.1 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v0-1-1" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.1.1 {#v0-1-1}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>June 6, 2026 · Discipline filters and bilingual use</p><h3 id="search-filters" tabindex="-1">Search filters <a class="header-anchor" href="#search-filters" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Search filters&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Added source-specific disciplines using OpenAlex Fields and Web of Science Categories.</li><li>Applied OpenAlex discipline filters to both initial retrieval and citation expansion.</li><li>Fixed handling of OpenAlex Field labels containing commas across the CLI, environment settings, API, and interface selections.</li></ul><h3 id="interface-and-packaging" tabindex="-1">Interface and packaging <a class="header-anchor" href="#interface-and-packaging" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Interface and packaging&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li>Added Chinese/English switching and refreshed user and deployment documentation.</li><li>Reorganized the community package around its self-contained core.</li><li>Included Docker/runtime packaging fixes, history improvements, and provider updates.</li></ul><p><a href="https://github.com/paperseek/paperseek/releases/tag/v0.1.1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Original release notes</a></p><h2 id="v0-1-0" tabindex="-1">0.1.0 <a class="header-anchor" href="#v0-1-0" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;0.1.0 {#v0-1-0}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>June 2, 2026 · First demo release</p><p>The first release established the literature-discovery workflow:</p><ul><li>Research questions in Chinese or English, LLM-generated queries, and iterative widening or narrowing based on source results.</li><li>Metadata collection and LLM relevance scores with brief explanations.</li><li>OpenAlex citation expansion and an interactive map with dragging, zooming, and panning.</li><li>Web results with search, filters, selection, and CSV export.</li><li>Local Web UI, command-line use, Docker deployment, and an optional Agent Skill.</li><li>Support for hosted model providers, compatible endpoints, and local Ollama.</li></ul><p>The demo release linked to its commit history without a separate feature list. This summary follows the <a href="https://github.com/paperseek/paperseek/blob/v0.1.0/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">README at the 0.1.0 tag</a>.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperseek/paperseek/releases/tag/v0.1.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Original release</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperseek/paperseek/commits/v0.1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Code history</a></p>',64)])])}const g=a(n,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
